hall I praise you in this? I praise you not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book-§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor I have received of the Lord that which also I delivered unto you, That the Lord Jesus the same night in which he was betrayed took bread:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡and when he had given thanks, he brake it, and said, Take, eat: this is my body, which is broken for you: this do in remembrance of me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«After the same manner also he took the cup, when he had supped, saying, This cup is the new testament in my blood: this do ye, as oft as ye drink it, in remembrance of me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`For as often as ye eat this bread, and drink this cup, ye do shew the Lord's death till he come.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book-§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆWherefore whosoever shall eat this bread, and drink this cup of the Lord, unworthily, shall be guilty of the body and blood of the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWBut let a man examine himself, and so let him eat of that bread, and drink of that cup.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuFor he that eateth and drinketh unworthily, eateth and drinketh damnation to himself, not discerning the Lord's body.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBFor this cause many are weak and sickly among you, and many sleep.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9For if we would judge ourselves, we should not be judged.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeBut when we are judged, we are chastened of the Lord, that we should not be condemned with the world.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book-§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse"¦verses’„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLWherefore, my brethren, when ye come together to eat, tarry one for another.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And if any man hunger, let him eat at home; that ye come not together unto condemnation. And the rest will I set in order when I come.¦layout ªlast_verse"